WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.253
Successful local inference depends on a few core terms.

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:07.457
A model file contains the data needed to run a trained model,

00:00:07.457 --> 00:00:09.558
commonly in GGUF format for llama.

00:00:09.558 --> 00:00:10.259
cpp workflows.

00:00:10.259 --> 00:00:14.463
The tokenizer converts text into tokens the model can process and converts

00:00:14.463 --> 00:00:16.214
generated tokens back into text.

00:00:16.214 --> 00:00:18.667
A prompt is the input you provide,

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:22.520
while the context window is the amount of prompt, conversation history,

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.023
and supporting text the model can consider during a run.

00:00:26.023 --> 00:00:29.176
Prompt processing and token generation are two different phases.

00:00:29.176 --> 00:00:33.380
Prompt processing is the work of reading and preparing the input context.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.182
Token generation is the step-by-step creation of output.

00:00:36.182 --> 00:00:40.736
A setup may process short prompts quickly but slow down with long context.

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:45.641
It may load a model successfully but generate slowly because the chosen model, quantization,

00:00:45.641 --> 00:00:48.443
hardware, or runtime settings are not well matched.

00:00:48.443 --> 00:00:50.195
Sampling settings shape the output.

00:00:50.195 --> 00:00:52.997
Temperature and related controls affect how deterministic, varied,

00:00:52.997 --> 00:00:54.749
or creative the result feels.

00:00:54.749 --> 00:00:56.851
Output length limits prevent runaway responses.

00:00:56.851 --> 00:01:00.704
Stop tokens help the runtime know when to end a completion.

00:01:00.704 --> 00:01:03.857
These settings do not make a weak model strong,

00:01:03.857 --> 00:01:08.061
but they can make a suitable model behave poorly if configured carelessly.

00:01:08.061 --> 00:01:11.564
CPU inference, GPU acceleration, and quantization are practical operating choices.

00:01:11.564 --> 00:01:15.768
CPU inference can be simple and portable but slower for larger models.

00:01:15.768 --> 00:01:19.971
GPU acceleration can improve speed when supported by hardware and runtime configuration.

00:01:19.971 --> 00:01:22.423
Quantization reduces memory requirements and file size,

00:01:22.423 --> 00:01:24.525
often with quality or behavior tradeoffs.

00:01:24.525 --> 00:01:27.328
Local inference works best when model, runtime, hardware,

00:01:27.328 --> 00:01:29.780
and configuration are treated as one system.
